Based on the retrieved code, JSON responses in Gin are HTML-escaped by default as a security measure. Here's why and how to turn it off:

## Why JSON is HTML-escaped

Looking at `render/json.go`, the standard `JSON` renderer uses Go's `json.Marshal()` which HTML-escapes characters like `<`, `>`, and `&` by default. For example:

```go
// From render/render_test.go
data := map[string]any{
    "foo":  "bar",
    "html": "<b>",
}
// Results in: {"foo":"bar","html":"\u003cb\u003e"}
```

The `<b>` gets escaped to `\u003cb\u003e` to prevent XSS attacks when JSON is embedded in HTML.

## How to turn off HTML-escaping

